A reactive loop whose body builds a box, on fyne.

The loop becomes a render slot, a Model method handed the container it renders
into. That parameter was called `container`, which is also the fyne package
the body calls to build an `hbox` -- so `container.NewHBox()` named the
parameter, and the program did not compile. It is `__parent` now.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `\(container \*fyne\.Container\)` -- the render slot's parameter would shadow the package its body calls
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
    }
}

window {
    var items = ["a", "b"]

    vbox {
        button(text="add", @click { items.push("c") })
        for var it = items {
            hbox {
                text(value="row {it}")
            }
        }
    }
}
-- out/go/fyne/model.go --
